{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"integrating 3 d with tracked video integrating 3 d with tracked video","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","fileName":"Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Integrating 3D with Tracked Video","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Motion Tracking]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Motion Tracking","Plate Lighting Reference for CG","Matching Moving Film Grain","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"integrating 3 d with tracked video integrating 3 d with tracked video","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","fileName":"Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Integrating 3D with Tracked Video","heading":"Integrating 3D with Tracked Video","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A tracked and oriented camera gives a Blender scene the perspective and movement of the recorded shot. Three-dimensional objects can then be placed against measured reference geometry so their position and scale match the footage.\n\nConvincing integration also depends on recreating the shot's lighting and combining render and footage in the Compositor. Camera background images are visible only through the camera and provide the immediate visual reference during placement.\n\nGress's plate-matching examples make the next checks explicit: compare key and fill direction, adjust RGB black/white/gamma levels, and reproduce atmospheric contrast and moving grain at the element's depth. A camera match alone does not prevent a pasted-on appearance. See [[Plate Lighting Reference for CG]] and [[Matching Moving Film Grain]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Motion Tracking","Plate Lighting Reference for CG","Matching Moving Film Grain","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"integrating 3 d with tracked video integrating 3 d with tracked video","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","fileName":"Integrating 3D with Tracked Video.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Integrating 3D with Tracked Video","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf]]\n[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Motion Tracking","Plate Lighting Reference for CG","Matching Moving Film Grain","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}